window.SNOWS_INDEX=[{"t":"Home","s":"Our Lady of the Snows Parochial School","u":"index.html","k":"home","f":0},{"t":"Catholic Identity","s":"Faith · The most essential difference between Catholic schools and public schools is the…","u":"our-faith/index.html","k":"Our school Charism, Mission Statement and School wide Learning Expectations strongly reflect our identity as a Catholic school. Each morning we begin our day with prayer at our morning assembly. While many of our students come from different faiths, we celebrate Mass together each Wednesday. The presence of sacred images are found in the classrooms and throughout our school. Weekly Wednesday Mass Our entire student body attends Mass celebrations each week. Individual classes are selected to prepare and proclaim scripture readings and prayer intentions for our weekly school Mass. Several studen","f":0},{"t":"Faith in Action","s":"Faith · Our students put their faith into action through a variety of service projects d…","u":"our-faith/faith-in-action/index.html","k":"Service projects expose students to opportunities to serve both locally and globally. These projects are developmentally appropriate for the different ages of students participating and give our students a deeper and broader understanding of what service truly means as they progress through their years here at Snows. Students at Our Lady of the Snows work to improve the lives of others by participating in a variety of service projects. Part of our SLEs and mission as a Catholic school is to take responsibility for the needs of others, locally and globally. Events that our children participate ","f":0},{"t":"Mass Schedule","s":"Faith · Parents are always warmly invited to participate in our school masses, held week…","u":"our-faith/mass-schedule/index.html","k":"School Mass Every Wednesday at 8:45am — in person at Our Lady of the Snows Parish and streamed live for families who can’t attend. Parish Mass Times The link below will direct you to the current Our Lady of the Snows Parish mass schedule. Mass Times for OLS Parish olsparish.com OLS School Mass YouTube Link Watch the live stream","f":1},{"t":"Sacraments","s":"Faith · Students preparing for the sacraments are accompanied by their families, their t…","u":"our-faith/sacraments/index.html","k":"The parents of students desiring sacraments attend a parent meeting beforehand and work with their child using the assigned text. After completing the text, students preparing for sacraments attend retreats for Reconciliation and First Communion. These retreats include Bible stories, crafts, review, and practice for each sacrament. Parents attend a sacramental preparation meeting. Families work through the assigned text together at home. Students attend retreats for Reconciliation and First Communion. Celebrate the sacrament with the Our Lady of the Snows community. Older children needing bapt","f":0},{"t":"Academics","s":"Academics · The academic focus of Our Lady of the Snows school is to inspire students to lov…","u":"academics/index.html","k":"This goal is achieved by engaging our students in challenging coursework that ignites their curiosity and develops competency in both arts and sciences. Snows students demonstrate strong critical thinking and communication skills and are consistently encouraged to meet their highest potential. Explore our program Accreditation Fully accredited by the Western Catholic Educational Association. Learn more → Learning Expectations Faith, Knowledge, Leadership and Service shape every classroom. See our SLEs → Curriculum Standards from the Archdiocese of Cincinnati and the State of Nevada. View curri","f":0},{"t":"Accreditation","s":"Academics · Our Lady of the Snows Catholic School is accredited by the Western Catholic Educ…","u":"academics/accreditation/index.html","k":"This accrediting body ensures that Catholic schools meet rigorous requirements in terms of both academic programs and Catholic identity. The requirements of the WCEA guide Our Lady of the Snows Catholic School to assess and strive for continual student improvement. The accrediting guidelines also ensure that academic curriculum incorporates the values taught in the Roman Catholic Church. Our Lady of the Snows underwent our 6-year accreditation visit in September of 2021 and actively worked with all members of our school community to create a self-study that guides our school action plan for th","f":0},{"t":"Schoolwide Learning Expectations","s":"Academics · Four promises every Snows student grows into: Faith, Knowledge, Leadership and S…","u":"academics/schoolwide-learning-expectations/index.html","k":"Faith I choose to have a personal relationship with God. • I know the prayers, Traditions, and teachings of the Catholic church • I make choices that reflect the Gospel message • I honor Mary as our Blessed Mother Knowledge I choose to always grow and learn. • I demonstrate competence in arts and sciences • I demonstrate critical thinking and problem solving skills • I demonstrate the ability to listen, speak, and write clearly Leadership I choose to be a positive influence in our community. • I model virtuous behavior • I take personal responsibility • I inspire others to be their best Servic","f":0},{"t":"Curriculum","s":"Academics · Standards for excellence — guided by our diocese, our Catholic faith and the Sta…","u":"academics/curriculum/index.html","k":"Standards for Excellence Our Lady of the Snows School received the highest level of achievement with a full 3– and 6-year accreditation from the Western Catholic Educational Association and the Western Association of Schools &amp; Colleges — joining only a handful of public and private schools to achieve such standards. In addition, the curriculum at Snows meets or exceeds all State regulations and guidelines. At Snows, we undergo regular accreditation certification to ensure continual improvement in an already excellent Catholic Educational environment. Our curriculum is guided by the standar","f":0},{"t":"Technology","s":"Academics · Technology Center — a multi-disciplinary environment where connections are made …","u":"academics/curriculum/technology/index.html","k":"Critical Thinking &amp; Problem Solving Project Management Collaboration &amp; Teamwork Communication Skills Creativity and Innovation Research Skills and Information Literacy Self-Direction &amp; Assessment It’s a simple and exciting strategy. Students of all abilities will engage in projects which capture their fascination with technology. These are challenging projects which are flexible, open-ended, and demand each child’s creativity. Result: Enriched learning with hands-on, minds-on curriculum supported by academically relevant exploration which will empower our students to explore topics","f":0},{"t":"Religion","s":"Academics · Grades kindergarten through eight follow the Finding God catechism series publis…","u":"academics/curriculum/religion/index.html","k":"This formal religious instruction curriculum meets all of the religious education standards of our Diocese. Beyond the textbook, students are immersed in a rich, faith filled school environment through our weekly participation in Mass and daily prayer. Each day begins with prayer and students learn a variety of styles of prayer from our Catholic tradition. Additionally, as a community we study the lives of the saints, each day, seeking inspiration and life lessons to help us all make Snows a place of learning, compassion and strong Catholic identity. As a school community we participate in a n","f":0},{"t":"Music & Enrichment","s":"Academics · Well-rounded students in today’s world must demonstrate competency in both the a…","u":"academics/curriculum/music-enrichment/index.html","k":"Through our music and enrichment programs we strive to build this competency and educate the whole child. Music is offered to grades K-8 on a weekly basis. In the Junior High, one period per day is dedicated to enrichment. Students rotate through courses in technology, careers, art and leadership. Weekly Music Offered to every grade from Kindergarten through 8th grade. Technology Junior High enrichment rotation. Careers & Art Exploring talents and future callings. Leadership Growing young leaders who serve.","f":0},{"t":"How We Measure Learning","s":"Academics · Student learning is assessed on an on-going basis through formal and informal cl…","u":"academics/how-we-measure-learning/index.html","k":"Results from these measures of learning are shared with parents regularly and are also used to continually improve instruction. Assessment is used at Our Lady of the Snows School to help us ensure that each child is making progress to the very best of his or her ability and reaching their highest potential. MAP Guide for Parents Measures of Academic Progress® creates a personalized assessment experience by adapting to each student’s learning level — precisely measuring student progress and growth for each student. Depending on how a student answers each question, the test adjusts in difficulty","f":0},{"t":"Student Life","s":"Student Life · Students at Our Lady of the Snows school are members of a faith-based community …","u":"student-life/index.html","k":"In addition to high academic expectations, students at Snows are also expected to share their unique personal gifts to enrich our school community. Whether it is service on the playground, in our parish or in our greater community and world, all students learn to give back and make our world a better place. Student life also includes the opportunity to participate in athletics through the CYO and in arts through music, drama and visual arts classes. Finally, students have many opportunities to develop their leadership skills, most notably in our Student Council and leadership workshops. CYO Le","f":0},{"t":"Before & After School Care","s":"Student Life · Boys & Girls Club @ Snows — safe, caring supervision before and after the school…","u":"student-life/before-after-school-care/index.html","k":"Before School Care Monday – Friday 7:00am – 8:30am Please do not drop off before this time. After School Care Monday – Friday 2:50pm – 5:45pm 12:15pm on early release days. Site Coordinator Email: snows@bgctm.org Phone: 775-324-8179 (only available during program hours) Please note: We are not open for snow days, holidays, or any breaks! However, we do feed into a Boys &amp; Girls Club Clubhouse for most days off/breaks. Please contact the Site Coordinator for more info. Registration Info Please go online to our website bgctm.org &amp; click “Join Now” to get your child registered. Watch the o","f":0},{"t":"CYO League Sports","s":"Student Life · Our Lady of the Snows encourages our students in 5th, 6th, 7th, and 8th grade to…","u":"student-life/cyo-league-sports/index.html","k":"These sports include volleyball and basketball for both boys and girls. Sign ups for different sports are announced in our Tuesday packet. CYO Volleyball CYO Volleyball is usually played in the Fall . CYO Basketball CYO Basketball is usually played in the Winter .","f":0},{"t":"Service","s":"Student Life · Service is a foundational piece of our school identity and our religion program …","u":"student-life/service/index.html","k":"Our students participate in a variety of service projects designed to give them hands-on, age appropriate opportunities to learn about Catholic social justice teachings. Our school service projects expose students to opportunities to serve both locally and globally. These projects aim to give students a deeper and broader understanding of what service truly means as they progress through their years here at Snows. Students at Our Lady of the Snows work to improve the lives of others by participating in a variety of service projects. Part of our SLEs and mission as a Catholic school is to take ","f":0},{"t":"Student Committees","s":"Student Life · Groups formed by leaders in the 8th grade class who want to be involved in extra…","u":"student-life/student-council/index.html","k":"The purpose of these groups is to foster strong leadership skills by encouraging student expression and promoting problem-solving and relationship-building. The 8th grade committees meet at various intervals throughout the year at which time school-wide issues will be addressed, decisions will be made, and information will be disseminated to the K-8 classes. Participants are responsible for spirit and community building activities throughout the year, including: Family events Catholic Schools Week Assemblies Service projects Middle school dances","f":0},{"t":"Supply Lists","s":"Student Life · Please find student grades, homework, and any information on financial accounts …","u":"student-life/supply-lists/index.html","k":"RenWeb Grades, homework &amp; accounts PDF School Calendar Supply List PDF Ms. Crowley’s Supply List PDF Melarkey Class List PDF Buxton Supply List PDF Romero Supply List 2026 PDF MS Supply List PDF School supplies 1,2,3,4 (2026) PDF 5th Grade School Supplies","f":0},{"t":"For Parents","s":"Parents · Our Lady of the Snows School places great value in partnering with our parents. …","u":"for-parents/index.html","k":"We recognize that we are most successful as a school when we integrate the wisdom, enthusiasm and experience of our parents as part of our educational approach. You are a vital part of our school community. New Parent Quick Links PDF School Calendar 2026 – 2027 Tuition and Fees Admission Application School Uniform Lunch Program Before and After School Care Protecting God’s Children Parent Student Handbook Supply Lists A day at Snows Schedule Time Morning Assembly 8:30 am Regular School Day (Monday – Thursday) 8:30 am – 2:50 pm Friday 8:30 am – 12:15 pm Early Release Days School ends at 12:15 p","f":0},{"t":"Vintage Affair","s":"Parents · Vintage Affair is our school’s premier fundraiser with the funds raised going to…","u":"vintage-affair/index.html","k":"Our annual gala brings together members of our school and parish community for a night of lively entertainment in support of our continued mission to guide and nurture our students to become young leaders who love God, love learning and love thy neighbor. Saturday, February 7, 2026 Reno Ballroom 400 N. Center Street Donate or Volunteer To donate to the silent auction or to volunteer, please email VA@SNOWSNV.ORG Event Information Follow us on Instagram @VintageAffair2026 Tickets, corporate sponsorship &amp; silent auction donations: please email VA@SNOWSNV.ORG and our gala team will help you. V","f":0},{"t":"Protecting God’s Children","s":"Parents · All adult volunteers at Our Lady of the Snows School must participate in the Pro…","u":"for-parents/protecting-gods-children/index.html","k":"Keeping every child safe. Completing these requirements is the first step before helping in classrooms, on field trips or at school events. Additional information regarding Volunteer work and Protecting God’s Children: PDF 3 Requirements to Volunteer Protecting God’s Children and Background Check Link","f":0},{"t":"School Uniform Ordering","s":"Parents · Snows uniforms are available from two official suppliers.…","u":"for-parents/school-uniform-policy/index.html","k":"Lands’ End School Number 900148032 800-469-2222 Shop Lands’ End → Search “School Uniforms” and enter our school number. Kate’s Logos 775-432-1222 1221 West 2nd Street, Reno, NV Shop Kate’s Logos → Uniform details are listed in the Student/Parent Handbook .","f":0},{"t":"Lunch Program","s":"Parents · Students at Snows may order hot lunch for $6.50 per lunch through Poi Boy Cateri…","u":"for-parents/lunch-program/index.html","k":"They will serve hot lunch “cafeteria” style daily and will offer pizza every Wednesday. Lunches are $6.50 daily. Log in to your account to view the menu. Please note: in consideration of our students with severe allergies, Our Lady of the Snows is a NUT FREE school. Please do not send lunches, snacks or treats with nuts to school. How to order Ordering is done completely online. They offer a “hot” option or a “cold” option daily. Please go to www.poiboycatering.com . You will see a tab for “school lunches”. Select that tab and it will lead you to the process of creating an account for your stu","f":1},{"t":"Parent Service Hours","s":"Parents · Families are partners in our community — service hours help make Snows thrive.…","u":"for-parents/parent-service-hours/index.html","k":"PDF Family Service Hours Information PDF Snows Field Trip Driver Application Protecting God’s Children and Background Check Link Looking for a way to serve? Watch the News &amp; Updates page and the Tuesday Packet for current opportunities.","f":0},{"t":"Mental Health","s":"Parents · All Schools in the Diocese of Reno will comply with SB 204, pertaining to Pupil …","u":"for-parents/mental-health/index.html","k":"Mental Health Resources include: Nevada Office of Suicide Prevention 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline Call or text 988, any time If your child needs support, please reach out to your child’s teacher or our school office at (775) 322-2773 . In an emergency, call or text 988 , the Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline.","f":0},{"t":"Student/Parent Handbook","s":"Parents · The Student Parent Handbook is updated every summer with policies and procedures…","u":"for-parents/student-parent-handbook/index.html","k":"PDF Parent Student Handbook 2026 – 2027 Information on topics such as our school discipline policy, bell schedule, uniform policy, homework policy, absences and tardies can all be found in this handbook. The handbook may also be accessed through RenWeb .","f":0},{"t":"Admissions","s":"Admissions · Registration for the 2026-2027 school year opened October 1, 2025. We would love…","u":"admissions/index.html","k":"Kindergarten Registration Registration for Kindergarten for the 2026-2027 school year will open October 1, 2025. You will need to submit the original birth certificate, original baptismal certificate and the most recent immunization records. Online Application — Click Here → Grades 1st – 8th Registration Applications for the 2026-2027 school year will open October 1, 2025. If there are any spots available, parents will be notified sometime in April 2026. Unfortunately, we do not have any openings for the current school year. Online Application Apply through RenWeb Enrollment Inquiry Email our ","f":1},{"t":"For Prospective Families","s":"Admissions · Our Lady of the Snows is proud to be an academically rigorous private service sc…","u":"admissions/for-prospective-families/index.html","k":"Through our strong sense of community and inspired by our Catholic Faith, Our Lady of the Snows School guides and nurtures our students to become young leaders who love God, love learning and love their neighbor. For any inquiries, please contact our office at 775.322.2773 . Your next steps Why Choose Us? Frequently Asked Questions Admissions Guidelines Tuition &amp; Fees Tuition Assistance Online Application","f":0},{"t":"Why Choose Us?","s":"Admissions · A place of learning, a place of faith, and a place where all are welcome.…","u":"admissions/why-choose-us/index.html","k":"Our Lady of the Snows School is proud of our reputation for providing a well rounded, academically challenging education for our students. But, of equal importance, Our Lady of the Snows strives to nurture the whole child; spiritually, physically and intellectually. Our Catholic values guide all aspects of our school life, creating a learning environment that respects the dignity of every individual. We work diligently to live our mission statement, nurturing our students to become young leaders who love God, love learning and love their neighbor. Our Lady of the Snows School is a place of lea","f":0},{"t":"Frequently Asked Questions","s":"Admissions · Answers to the questions families ask us most.…","u":"admissions/frequently-asked-questions/index.html","k":"Are all teachers licensed and credentialed? Yes. Following the guidelines of the Diocese of Reno, all of our academic teachers are licensed and credentialed. Are extra-curricular activities offered? Snows students can participate in a variety of extra-curricular activities ranging from sports through CYO to scouting groups, chess club, youth ministry and service groups and leadership workshops. Opportunities vary and information on what is currently available may be found by contacting our school office or in our weekly school newsletter. Do I need to be Catholic? The Catholic faith is integra","f":0},{"t":"Testimonials","s":"Admissions · In the words of our Snows families.…","u":"admissions/testimonials/index.html","k":"“My husband and I are very happy with Our Lady of the Snows School. Our 2 children love it and are learning a lot. The principal is very involved with the children and the teachers and staff are wonderful! We plan to send our youngest there as well when she is old enough.” — Parent “We are very happy at Our Lady of the Snows. My wife and I were recommended by many families that are presently attending and have graduated. We are grateful to have found OLS.” — P. Bertone “My three children graduated from this school and would recommend it to anyone. The teachers, staff and principal are fantasti","f":0},{"t":"Admissions Guidelines","s":"Admissions · Our Lady of the Snows School seeks to admit students whose families desire not o…","u":"admissions/admissions-guidelines/index.html","k":"Successful students at Snows will share the Catholic values reflected in our schoolwide learning expectations . They should be willing to live out our mission statement and both students and parents should be willing to participate in and enrich our learning community. Faith Share in the Catholic values that shape our school. Learning Embrace a strong, challenging academic setting. Community Participate in and enrich our learning community.","f":0},{"t":"Tuition & Fees","s":"Admissions · 2026 – 2027 Tuition Rates…","u":"admissions/tuition-fees/index.html","k":"New Family Registration $750 per family, per year, non-refundable Returning Family Registration $650 per family, per year, non-refundable Active Parishioner Grade Annual Rate 11 monthly payments Kindergarten $8,275 per child $752 1st thru 5th Grade $7,485 per child $680 6th – 8th Grade $7,685 per child $699 Non-Active / Non-Parishioner Grade Annual Rate 11 monthly payments Kindergarten $9,345 per child $850 1st thru 5th Grade $8,960 per child $815 6th – 8th Grade $9,160 per child $833 Sibling Discount: $400 per second and third students (as applicable) excluding Kindergarteners. An “Active Par","f":1},{"t":"Tuition Assistance","s":"Admissions · A limited amount of Tuition Assistance is available to selected applicants after…","u":"admissions/tuition-assistance/index.html","k":"Due to the review process, late packets are not accepted. In order to be considered for Tuition Assistance or the D.O.R.S. Scholarship parents MUST apply for at least one Nevada Choice Scholarship. For information on how to apply for a Nevada Choice Scholarship please visit the State of Nevada Department of Education website. Due date: May 31, 2027 , for the 2027 – 2028 school year. FACTS Grant &amp; Aid Assessment conducts the financial needs analysis of each application for Our Lady of the Snows. Families applying for financial aid will need to complete an application and submit the necessar","f":0},{"t":"Nevada Choice Scholarships","s":"Admissions · The Nevada Educational Choice Scholarship Program (AB 165) allows corporations t…","u":"admissions/nevada-choice-scholarships/index.html","k":"Up to $ 10,367 for the 2026 – 2027 school year, based upon household income. Approved School Our Lady of the Snows School is an approved school to receive these funds. These scholarships can be used for Kindergarten through 12th grade and have no basis on public school attendance! We strongly encourage all eligible families to apply for this scholarship. Below is the link to the State of Nevada website that contains links to the organizations that are accepting applications: State of Nevada – Nevada Choice Scholarships","f":0},{"t":"About Snows","s":"About · Inspired by our Catholic Faith, Our Lady of the Snows School guides and nurtures…","u":"about/index.html","k":"1951 Year Opened K – 8 Grades 360 Enrollment 29 Number of Faculty Roman Catholic Religious Affiliation The Falcon School Mascot Principal’s Message Tim Fuetsch Principal · Reno, Nevada It has been my great privilege to serve as Principal of Our Lady of the Snows School for the past fifteen years. I have great pride in our school community and in the academic excellence and faith formation that we offer to our students. During my time as Principal, our staff, students and parents have worked hard to build a community that is a true reflection of our Catholic faith. We are a school that welcomes","f":0},{"t":"Enrollment & Facilities","s":"About · A campus designed for faith, learning and community.…","u":"about/enrollment-facilities/index.html","k":"Our facilities include Our Lady of the Snows Parish, Our Lady of the Snows School with multi age classrooms in Elementary grades, a Middle School wing, an updated Library, Resource Classroom, Music Room, and outdoor space for students and families. Parish Church Our Lady of the Snows Parish, home of our weekly school Mass. Updated Library Renovated with a modern check-out system. Chromebook for Every Student Daily digital learning, security and citizenship. Music Room Weekly music for every grade. Middle School Wing Dedicated space for grades 7 and 8. Mesh Wi-Fi &amp; New HVAC Modern infrastru","f":0},{"t":"School History","s":"About · For over seventy years, Our Lady of the Snows School has consistently built a le…","u":"about/school-history/index.html","k":"1950s — Our Beginning On September 4, 1951, Our Lady of the Snows Catholic School first opened its doors under the direction of Msgr. Patrick J. Connors to meet the needs of our growing parish. With 107 students and four classrooms, our School was led by two Dominican Sisters and one lay teacher. By 1953, four additional classrooms and a social hall were added. Our School was blessed by the Bishop in 1956 and the first graduation exercises were held with 21 students receiving diplomas. 1960s The library was added to the existing structure and facilities were redesigned with entrances from the ","f":0},{"t":"Mission","s":"About · Love God. Love learning. Love each other.…","u":"about/mission/index.html","k":"Inspired by our Catholic Faith, Our Lady of the Snows School guides and nurtures students to become young leaders who love God, love learning and love each other. Love God A personal relationship with God, nurtured by daily prayer, weekly Mass and the sacraments. Love Learning Challenging coursework that ignites curiosity in the arts and sciences. Love Each Other Service, compassion and leadership — locally and globally. Our mission comes to life through our Schoolwide Learning Expectations : Faith, Knowledge, Leadership and Service.","f":0},{"t":"Contact","s":"About · We would love to hear from you — and to show you our campus in person.…","u":"about/contact/index.html","k":"Address 1125 Lander St. Reno, NV 89509 Get directions → Phones Phone: (775) 322-2773 Fax: (775) 322-0827 Email info@snowsnv.org More ways to connect Communications Important Links &amp; How To’s Faculty &amp; Staff Directory Employment Opportunities","f":1},{"t":"Communications","s":"About · Our Lady of the Snows communicates with our parents through our Tuesday Packet.…","u":"about/contact/communications/index.html","k":"Tuesday Packet This electronic newsletter is sent out weekly and is our primary source for letting our school families know what is going on from week to week at our school and in our parish and community. Snows News On a bi-monthly basis we also have a school newsletter, Snows News, which offers information to help families with timely educational topics. Personal Communication We place a high value on personal communication and encourage meetings with teachers and administrators to address problems and concerns. RenWeb is our school management site where parents can find information on curre","f":0},{"t":"Important Links","s":"About · Quick access to the sites our families use most.…","u":"about/contact/important-links-how-tos/index.html","k":"Our Lady of the Snows Church Diocese of Reno RenWeb Login Bishop Manogue Catholic High School FACTS Tuition Management","f":0},{"t":"Faculty & Staff Directory","s":"About · School starts every day at 8:30am. School hours 8:30am – 2:50pm (Mon – Thurs) & …","u":"about/contact/faculty-staff-directory/index.html","k":"Reach the school office at (775) 322-2773 or info@snowsnv.org . All Administration Classroom Teachers Specialists Aides Operations Fr. Bob Chorey Pastor 775-323-6894 x 510 Tim Fuetsch Principal 775-322-2773 x551 Jessie Cartinella Assistant Principal Heather Parks Secretary David Shore Information Technology 775-322-2773 x555 Lorinda Maez Bookkeeper 775-322-2773 x552 Kelsey Melarkey Kindergarten Teacher Storm Buxton Kindergarten Teacher Leslie Crouser 1-2 Image Class Teacher Kathy Hogan 1-2 Image Class Teacher Jessica Simpson 1-2 Image Class Teacher Jayme Drescher 3rd Grade Teacher Olivia Dolan","f":0},{"t":"Employment Opportunities","s":"About · Join a faith-filled team dedicated to forming young leaders who love God, love l…","u":"about/contact/employment-opportunities/index.html","k":"For application, please click here Diocese of Reno employment Questions? Email info@snowsnv.org","f":0},{"t":"Legal Notices","s":"About · Required notices and compliance documents.…","u":"about/mission-2/index.html","k":"Nevada Department of Education Emergency Operations Plan: PDF Notice of Completion","f":0},{"t":"Welcome Home Project","s":"Welcome Home · To date we have received $14,600,000.00 in pledges toward our goal of $19 millio…","u":"welcome-home-project/index.html","k":"Welcome to Commitment Weekend! The formal push for our Welcome Home project is winding down and we continue to be amazed by the generosity of the Our Lady of the Snows community. We kicked off our effort four weeks ago and since then we have seen the fundraising totals gradually climb. While this is great progress there is still much work ahead of us to reach our ultimate goal of $19 million to ensure we can begin construction on the new Our Lady of the Snows Family Center. We are now asking you to celebrate Commitment Weekend. It is important to honor the families who have given so generously","f":0},{"t":"Goal: Pledges To Date","s":"Welcome Home · As we continue through the public phase of our Welcome Home Capital Campaign, we…","u":"goal-pledges-to-date/index.html","k":"Pledges to date $ 14.6 M of our $19,000,000 goal All registered families should have received an information packet and a pledge card. Please prayerfully consider the level of support you can make to this campaign to build the new Snows Family Center. Two convenient ways to pledge support: Complete your paper pledge form and return it to the parish office or collection basket during Mass. Access the online giving page by scanning this QR code with the camera of your smartphone or tablet, or click here to give online . Thank you for your prayerful consideration of a gift to this important effor","f":0},{"t":"Vision: Building","s":"Welcome Home · A new Snows Family Center — space to welcome, serve, build, form and continue ou…","u":"vision-building/index.html","k":"The Welcome Home Project serves to create the infrastructure we need to welcome, serve, build, form and continue our mission as Catholics. Here is what the new Parish Center will make possible for our school and parish families. Gathering Space Graduations, the Christmas Program, Mother’s Day Tea, Family Game Nights, Fall Festival, assemblies, indoor recess/PE and more. Dedicated Classrooms Smaller class sizes, religious education, youth ministry and adult faith formation. Safe Pick-Up Loop A safer drop-off and pick-up for school children and parents. Accessible Offices ADA compliant access, s","f":0},{"t":"How To Donate","s":"Welcome Home · Online Giving powered by WeShare. Thank you for your generous support. God Bless…","u":"how-to-donate/index.html","k":"Step 1 Step 2 Step 3 Prefer another way to give? Visit WeShare Online Giving or contact the parish office.","f":0},{"t":"News and Updates","s":"Snows · The latest happenings, traditions and opportunities at Our Lady of the Snows.…","u":"news-and-updates/index.html","k":"March 27, 2026 9th – 12th Grade Upcoming Events Important upcoming events and information for families of students heading into 9th – 12th grade. Read More → February 25, 2026 The Traveling Mary is a great tradition we have at School. It brings the Faith based aspect of our school into your home… Read More → February 25, 2026 Service Hour Opportunity – Next Thursday, March 5 Still looking for a way to earn service hours? On Thursday, March 5… Read More → February 24, 2026 Hats Off to Reading Read Across America week starts March 9th here at OLS!… Read More →","f":0},{"t":"Calendar of Events 2026 - 2027","s":"Snows · Upcoming events, holidays and milestones for the 2026 – 2027 school year.…","u":"calendar-of-events/index.html","k":"PDF Download 2026 – 2027 Calendar Upcoming Events October 2026 16 OCT Parent Conferences Friday, October 16, 2026 School Event 23 OCT Parent Conferences Friday, October 23, 2026 School Event 23 OCT End of Q1 Friday, October 23, 2026 Academics 27 OCT Make-up Pictures Tuesday, October 27, 2026 School Event 30 OCT Parent Conferences Friday, October 30, 2026 School Event 30 OCT Nevada Day - No School Friday, October 30, 2026 No School November 2026 11 NOV Veterans Day - No School Wednesday, November 11, 2026 No School 23 NOV Thanksgiving Break Monday, November 23, 2026 No School December 2026 1 DE","f":1},{"t":"9th – 12th Grade Upcoming Events","s":"News · 9th - 12th Grade Upcoming Events…","u":"2026/03/27/9th-12th-grade-upcoming-events/index.html","k":"9th - 12th Grade Upcoming Events","f":0},{"t":"The Traveling Mary is a great tradition we have at School.","s":"News · It brings the Faith based aspect of our school into your home. Please sign up be…","u":"2026/02/25/the-traveling-mary-is-a-great-tradition-we-have-at-school/index.html","k":"It brings the Faith based aspect of our school into your home. Please sign up below to take the statue of Mary home for 1 week on Wednesday at the end of mass. This is a great way to pray together as a family, and also a great way to get ready for the Season of Lent. There are plenty of spots open for 2 families to take the Mary statue home every week. All families are welcome! Click on the link below to sign up Traveling Mary Sign Up via Flocknote","f":0},{"t":"Service Hour Opportunity – Next Thursday, March 5","s":"News · Still looking for a way to earn service hours? On Thursday, March 5 we’ll need m…","u":"2026/02/25/service-hour-opportunity-next-thursday-march-5/index.html","k":"Still looking for a way to earn service hours? On Thursday, March 5 we’ll need mid-day coverage for our teachers and student teachers who will be celebrating Teacher For A Day. We’re looking for volunteers to help with lunch and recess coverage between 11:30am and 1pm. You can earn 2 hours for a 1.5 hour shift! Sign up here to help! Teacher For A Day — SignUpGenius","f":0},{"t":"Hats Off to Reading","s":"News · Read Across America week starts March 9th here at OLS! More info to follow in li…","u":"2026/02/24/hats-off-to-reading/index.html","k":"Read Across America week starts March 9th here at OLS! More info to follow in library classes this week and next, however, I wanted to let everyone know about the OLS Book Swap on Friday March 13. This is a great way to get kids involved in donating books they have outgrown. I am asking for each child to donate 2 gently used/read books that they already own. At the end of Read Across America week, OLS students will be able to walk through and each pick out a “new to them” book! All the extras will be donated to a local elementary school here in Reno for their students to pick and take home a f","f":0}];
